&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Elastic, the Search AI Company, enables everyone to find the answers they need in real time, using all their data, at scale — unleashing the potential of businesses and people. The Elastic Search AI Platform, used by more than 50% of the Fortune 500, brings together the precision of search and the intelligence of AI to enable everyone to accelerate the results that matter. By taking advantage of all structured and unstructured data — securing and protecting private information more effectively — Elastic’s complete, cloud-based solutions for search, security, and observability help organizations deliver on the promise of AI.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re eager to welcome an outstanding Product Manager to join the Elastic Observability product team, with a focus on logs and logs analytics capabilities. With your knowledge and understanding of the Observability domain, you&#39;ll help ensure that we give our customers the best end to end full stack Observability experience for logs we collect from the applications and infrastructure we monitor. This role significantly impacts the success of our Observability product!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolving our logs analytics capabilities, aligning at every step with organizational and company strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advancing and influencing the entire end-to-end lifecycle for logs collection, ingest, and management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building features that cater to the modern SRE. From integrating GenAI and Agentic workflows into the logging experience, automated SLO/SLI tracking from logs, intelligent alerting, correlating logs, metrics, and traces, and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely across teams, collaborating with Engineering, UX, Design and other teams to bring top notch application monitoring experiences to our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with our Sales &amp;amp; Marketing teams on go-to-market, messaging, competitive analysis, enablement, and feature adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tracking user engagement and feedback to inform product and feature evolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideally 3+ years in product management or closely related area&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical experience in logs analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability and/or performance monitoring domain knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with and converting abstract problems into concrete, prioritized solutions, working from the customer backwards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding spoken and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for industry trends, competitive landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in remote, globally distributed work environment is optional but desired&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of AI is optional but desired&lt;/li&gt;
